  ],
  "details": "<p><em>Tribus Clustumina</em> or <em>Crustumina</em> was one of the older rural tribes of Rome. Its name derives from the site of Crustumerium on the Tiber river north of Fidenae in a region later known as the <em>ager Crustuminus</em>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Clustumina (or Crustumina) was a rural tribe of Rome which was established in 495 B.C.",
